2. Procedure
3. Opened Command Prompt and verified Docker installation.
4. Verified kubectl installation.
5. Verified Minikube installation.
6. Started Minikube using the Docker driver.
7. Checked Minikube status and verified the Kubernetes node was in Ready state.
8. Created a YAML file named nginx-pod.yaml using Notepad.
9. Configured the Pod with the Nginx image and container port 80.
10. Applied the YAML configuration using kubectl apply -f nginx-pod.yaml.
11. Checked the Pod status using kubectl get pods.
12. Displayed detailed Pod information using kubectl describe pod nginx-pod.
13. Forwarded the Pod port to localhost using kubectl port-forward.
14. Opened http://localhost:8081 in the browser and verified the Nginx Welcome page.
15. Stopped port forwarding and deleted the Pod using kubectl delete pod nginx-pod.
